{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Tell me, pray, etc.</b> One needs to know how he knew that the one asking him knew where they were pasturing, so as to say to him plainly, ״Tell me, pray.״ Or perhaps he scrutinized the words of the questioner in his saying, ״to say: What do you seek?״ — for the word ״to say״ is superfluous. He intended to say: when he asked him, it was so that he would tell him what he was seeking — for otherwise there is no place for a stranger who is not his brother to ask to know what he is seeking. Rather, he meant that his questioner wished to tell him a matter hidden from him, and therefore he answered him, ״I seek my brothers,״ and your words now come to tell me where they are pasturing."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:32.166299640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}